### Owned restart health foundation (2026-10-10)

The actual service entrypoint now answers an exact private IPC nonce challenge
only while ready and after a bounded fresh local runtime check. The installer
adapter verifies its actual child PID, runtime instance, product version and
nonce; startup acknowledgements or stale runtime records cannot satisfy it.
Cancellation and deadlines clean up probe listeners without killing the app
or releasing installation ownership.

A real silent service subprocess passed the fresh challenge and retained its
local data marker. Focused tests reject malformed/foreign IPC replies, wrong
versions/PIDs, overlapping probes, cancelled probes and unresponsive channels.
The runtime also reports not-ready immediately while shutdown drains a held
settings writer. These portable checks do not prove a completed update.

The independent installer supervisor, complete persistent-writer composition,
trusted production signing/release artifacts, restart/rollback composition
and EN/ES installation controls still require implementation and acceptance.
Native Mac/Safari assurance remains in the final ongoing record.

### Owned shutdown completion (2026-10-10)

The actual service entrypoint now accepts an exact private installer stop
challenge for its runtime instance. It replies after managed local/online
writer drainage and then closes its IPC channel. The parent requires a matching
nonce/version/instance/PID receipt plus successful final child closure; signal
delivery, disconnect and parent exit alone cannot authorize an exchange.

Deadline or cancelled observation retains an opaque pending completion and its
listeners until closure. Concurrent identical requests share completion;
conflicting challenges are refused without sending another stop. No timer
kills the app or releases installation ownership.

Real service subprocess tests prove silent stop, fresh restart and preserved
local data. A real managed service with an injected held settings writer keeps
its lock through the deadline and saves the admitted change before completion.
Synthetic real-IPC tests reject malformed/foreign receipts and failed exits;
an inherited open pipe prevents premature completion after parent exit.
These are portable managed-service guarantees.

Independent CLI-writer fencing,
installer lifetime, authenticated app selection, production publisher artifacts
and local opt-in installation/recovery controls remain required.


### Canonical user-data writer exclusion (2026-10-10)

Canonical library, personal-skill and draft commands now retain a private
per-operation lease from before preference/library initialization until actual
command completion. This includes read commands whose first use creates local
state. Pure instruction-profile retrieval remains independent of user storage.
Registered commands can complete concurrently; only bounded registration
metadata contention is retried before any command/native writer starts.

The local updater can acquire exclusive command admission only after a bounded
private lease scan finds no admitted or orphaned writer. Its installation
marker is never reclaimed merely because the supervisor PID is dead; a retained
native descendant may still be writing. Unknown, symbolic, publicly accessible
and oversized lease storage refuses installation without deleting evidence.

Real CLI tests refuse a personal-skill save while update admission is held and
preserve teacher data. Separate child processes demonstrate active command
exclusion, retained leases after abrupt writer death, and blocked commands after
installer death. Concurrent registrations remain independently usable.
The [Node filesystem documentation][node-filesystem-current] was checked on
the same date for bounded directory iteration and iterator-owned closure.

This fences canonical user-data commands, not every persistent writer.
Composition still must join the direct UI/settings/lifecycle leases, hold the
publication boundary first, supervise the installer independently, authenticate
production artifacts, and implement opt-in install/recovery controls before
enabling replacement. Native platform-only assurance remains in blooket-15.

### Private installer-child startup (2026-10-13)

The actual service entrypoint can accept a bounded private IPC startup request
from its installer parent. Issuance requires the live held data boundary and
the actual connected child; child admission verifies its own PID, actual parent
PID and confidential ownership against the private installation marker.
Neither a decoded message, argument, environment value nor stale PID alone
grants this exception. A readiness notice only ensures the IPC listener exists.

Real silent subprocess tests prove startup and fresh private health while
ordinary data operations remain refused, preserved teacher data after drained
shutdown, and exclusion of another installation while the candidate runs.
Foreign owners/tokens/children, extra fields, absent IPC and released/fabricated
boundary capabilities cannot obtain startup authority. Bounded deadline and
malformed-message tests remove observation listeners without killing a service.

This completes the private candidate-startup primitive, not independent
supervisor/recovery composition, trusted production release publication or
opt-in product controls. These remain functional requirements before closing
this record; Mac/Safari execution remains only in the evergreen assurance task.

### Independent managed service supervisor (2026-10-13)

The normal launcher now starts an independent silent supervisor that retains
the actual service child and IPC after the launcher exits. Startup readiness
requires fresh owned health; a launcher timeout neither kills the service nor
claims writer completion. A managed drainage notice from UI shutdown triggers
a fresh private stop challenge, then joins the service child's final closure.
Supervisor stop signals use the same challenge without killing service
writers.

Real launcher/subprocess tests demonstrate duplicate reuse, availability after
launcher disconnect, completed UI and supervisor shutdown, preserved teacher
data and released lifecycle admission. The disconnected launcher observes only
supervisor exit, keeping private receipt plus actual service closure mandatory
for installation proof. The [Node parent-disconnect issue][node-disconnect]
was checked against a local Node 24.18.0 reproduction on the same date.

Independent normal supervision is now composed into startup. Immutable helper
preparation, trusted production publisher/release configuration, transactional
installation/recovery composition and opt-in EN/ES controls remain functional
work. These tests do not claim native Mac/Safari execution or a completed
update.

